{
  "$schema": "internal://bridges-test-scenarios/v1",
  "_readme": [
    "Source of truth for the testnet bridge tests. Read by `scripts/testnet.ts`.",
    "",
    "WHY MOST VALUES ARE OMITTED: almost nothing here needs to be hardcoded.",
    "  - CCTP's quote API takes only *domain ids*, never contract addresses.",
    "  - LI.FI takes chain ids and token addresses, and resolves tokens itself",
    "    via `getTokens(chainId)`.",
    "  - Only LayerZero needs a contract address (the OApp being called), because",
    "    the fee belongs to that OApp rather than to LayerZero globally.",
    "So this file carries identifiers and endpoints, and the harness resolves",
    "the rest. Hardcoded addresses would be values that silently rot.",
    "",
    "`wallet.name` is the human label shown in logs (the 'contact name'), so a",
    "pending transfer can be discussed without quoting a hex string.",
    "",
    "`results` is WRITTEN BY THE HARNESS, not by hand. A run records the tx",
    "hashes it produced so a re-run can resume polling a transfer already in",
    "flight instead of sending a second one."
  ],
  "chains": {
    "sepolia": {
      "label": "Ethereum Sepolia",
      "chainId": 11155111,
      "cctpDomain": 0,
      "lzEid": 40161,
      "rpcEnv": "ETHEREUM_RPC_URL",
      "bridgeChain": "EthereumSepolia"
    },
